Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: end the forward path at an AP interface

ieee80211_netdev_fill_forward_path() fails with -EOPNOTSUPP when the
driver has no net_fill_forward_path op, as ath12k. dev_fill_forward_path()
then drops the whole path, and a flowtable entry for a station behind
a bridge keeps the bridge as its output device. Hardware flow offload
(the Qualcomm PPE) cannot use that and rejects the flow.

For an AP or AP_VLAN interface with a known station, end the path at
the interface itself as a plain Ethernet hop instead.

Signed-off-by: Timofey Maykov <itnitro@gmail.com>
---
--- a/net/mac80211/iface.c	2026-09-30 21:26:50.527501584 +0000
+++ b/net/mac80211/iface.c	2026-09-30 21:26:50.539817459 +0000
@@ -997,7 +997,9 @@
 	sdata = IEEE80211_DEV_TO_SUB_IF(ctx->dev);
 	local = sdata->local;
 
-	if (!local->ops->net_fill_forward_path)
+	if (!local->ops->net_fill_forward_path &&
+	    sdata->vif.type != NL80211_IFTYPE_AP &&
+	    sdata->vif.type != NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN)
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 
 	rcu_read_lock();
@@ -1037,6 +1039,18 @@
 	if (!sta)
 		goto out;
 
+	/* Without a hardware path in the driver the frame still leaves
+	 * through this interface. End the path here, so that a bridge
+	 * above keeps its resolved port instead of losing the whole path.
+	 */
+	if (!local->ops->net_fill_forward_path) {
+		path->type = DEV_PATH_ETHERNET;
+		path->dev = ctx->dev;
+		ctx->dev = NULL;
+		ret = 0;
+		goto out;
+	}
+
 	ret = drv_net_fill_forward_path(local, sdata, &sta->sta, ctx, path);
 out:
 	rcu_read_unlock();
